The audience is first-time, never-licensed Vermont applicants, typically teenagers on the learner's permit and junior license path and adults applying for a first driver's license, reading at a plain-English level with no assumed driving vocabulary. This section teaches crossbuck and slow moving vehicle signs, how warning and regulatory signs are shaped and colored, what yellow and white lines allow, two way left turn lanes, yield lines, lane use control, and how to drive through a work zone including flaggers, channeling devices, arrow panels and temporary markings. The content assumes no prior rule knowledge and no prerequisites beyond literacy; every term the section introduces is defined in the glossary lines of part C.
